.TH passwd 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
passwd \- change a password
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B passwd
[\fIname\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B passwd
changes the password of
.IR name ,
or of the user running it.  It asks for the old password first unless
the superuser is running it, then for the new one twice.
.PP
An ordinary user may only change their own password.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/passwd
Where the password is kept.  FUZIX has no shadow file: the hashes are in
this world-readable file, as they were in V7.
.SH NOTES
A machine on a network with a readable
.B /etc/passwd
is not a machine to reuse a password on.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR su (1),
.BR id (1),
.BR logname (1)
